Node's `url.URL` is the global WHATWG `URL`, so `fileURLToPath(new URL("./x.js",
import.meta.url))` is the documented way to find a file next to a module. Inside
`declare module "url"`, `URL` names the module's own class, so a global `new URL(...)`
was refused. Name the global before the module and accept it as well. Remove after
the upstream declaration accepts the global URL.

